  "intro": "Ramp, Mercury, Expensify, BILL and Relay are the five Brex alternatives for business cards and spend management covered here. Published software prices across these options run from $0 entry plans on Ramp Free, Mercury, Expensify Submit and Relay Starter to $299 per month on Mercury Pro and $89 per user per month on BILL Corporate. At The Modern Wallet, we lay out published fee structures so teams can compare corporate cards and expense controls across a full year.\n\n[Brex](https://www.brex.com/pricing) sells two main published tiers: Essentials at $0 per user per month and Premium at $12 per user per month, alongside custom pricing on Enterprise and Smart Card tiers. Brex LLC operates as a wholly owned subsidiary of Capital One, N.A., and its page notes that plans start at $0 per user per month while more advanced features cost $12 per user per month. Brex displays variable annualized estimated treasury return figures ranging from 3.63% to 3.98%.\n\nTo place spend tools within your broader financial stack, review our [best business bank accounts roundup](/roundup/best-business-bank-accounts/) and our [best business credit cards roundup](/roundup/best-business-credit-cards/). If your operations also require bookkeeping or invoicing software, explore our [best accounting software for freelancers](/roundup/best-accounting-software-for-freelancers/) guide, our [Mercury alternatives](/alternatives/mercury/) breakdown, our [Novo alternatives](/alternatives/novo/) review, and the central [comparison hub](/compare/).",
