  "chooseSection": {
    "heading": "How to Choose a Brex Alternative",
    "body": "Start by identifying whether your business needs dedicated corporate card and spend management software, an integrated commercial checking account with built-in cards, or a focused accounts payable application. Brex combines corporate charge cards, bill pay, employee reimbursements and travel booking into one platform. Brex provides an entry tier at $0 per user per month and charges $12 per user per month on Premium for custom expense policies and deeper enterprise resource planning (ERP) connections. Evaluating alternatives requires checking fee models, user seat charges, banking features and multi-entity support.\n\nFirst, assess the billing unit. Brex charges on a per-user, per-month schedule on Premium ($12 per user per month). For a team with 10 employees, Brex Premium costs $12 multiplied by 10 users multiplied by 12 months, which equals $1,440 per year. Brex Essentials costs $0. In comparison, Ramp offers a Free plan at $0 per user per month and a Plus tier at $15 per user per month plus an unpublished platform fee based on team size, with an advertised 20% savings on annual billing. Expensify Collect charges $5 per member per month, which equals $600 per year for 10 users ($5 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12). BILL charges $49 per user per month on Essentials ($5,880 per year for 10 users), $65 per user per month on Team ($7,800 per year), and $89 per user per month on Corporate ($10,680 per year), while stating no per-user subscription fees for BILL Spend & Expense. Mercury and Relay charge flat monthly platform rates regardless of user headcount, with Mercury base at $0 per month and Relay Starter at $0 per month with unlimited user seats.\n\nSecond, evaluate banking and cash management structures. Brex LLC is listed as a wholly owned subsidiary of Capital One, N.A. Brex displays estimated annualized treasury returns between 3.63% and 3.98%. If your team requires a business checking account directly attached to card issuance, Mercury provides up to $5M in Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation (FDIC) coverage through partner banks and sweep networks, free Automated Clearing House (ACH) transfers, free domestic and United States Dollar (USD) international wires, and treasury access starting at a $250,000 balance. Ramp lists earning 2% on cash held in an FDIC-insured checking account and 4.66% in a Ramp Investment Account under variable footnoted terms. Relay offers checking accounts with tiered savings yields: 1.19% Annual Percentage Yield (APY) on Starter, 1.87% APY on Grow ($30 per month), and 3.21% APY on Scale ($120 per month shown alongside $90).\n\nThird, examine multi-entity and accounting system requirements. Brex Essentials supports up to two business entities, while Brex Premium expands to multi-entity management across domestic and international operations. Ramp Free provides standard accounting sync with QuickBooks Online and Xero, while NetSuite and Sage Intacct integrations require Ramp Plus alongside multi-entity support. Expensify supports QuickBooks and Xero on Collect ($5 per member per month) and reserves NetSuite and Sage Intacct for Control. BILL Essentials syncs through comma-separated values (CSV) file imports and exports, requiring Team or Corporate for automatic accounting sync.\n\nFour concrete criteria to check:\n\n- How many employees need active cards or review permissions, and what is the total per-seat monthly cost?\n- Does your business require multi-entity consolidation across international subsidiaries?\n- Does your finance workflow require built-in business checking, or do you connect external bank accounts?\n- Which accounting software or ERP system must synchronize with transaction data?"
  },
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "heading": "Ramp Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Ramp provides corporate cards, expense management, bill payment and travel booking. Its Free plan lists at $0 per user per month. The Free plan includes unlimited corporate cards, travel and expense management, budgets, financial reporting, accounts payable supporting bill payments through ACH, check, card and wire, and direct integrations with QuickBooks Online and Xero. Ramp also notes earning 2% on cash in an FDIC-insured checking account and 4.66% in a Ramp Investment Account under footnoted variable terms.\n\nRamp Plus costs $15 per user per month plus a platform fee determined by team size, with an advertised 20% savings when billed annually. Ramp Plus adds multi-entity support, artificial intelligence (AI) expense reviews, and integrations with NetSuite and Sage Intacct, while procurement capabilities are offered as a separate add-on. Ramp Enterprise operates under custom pricing on annual contracts.\n\nWorked cost example: For an organization with 10 users on Ramp Plus, the per-seat charge is 10 multiplied by $15 multiplied by 12 months, which equals $1,800 per year before adding the team-size platform fee, which is unpublished on the pricing page. On Brex Premium, that same 10-user group costs $12 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12, or $1,440 per year. Both providers list $0 tiers for core features, where 10 users cost $0 on Brex Essentials and $0 on Ramp Free. These figures represent list-price arithmetic for 10 users, not formal quotes.\n\nRamp fits companies seeking corporate cards and accounts payable with no subscription fee on the Free tier. Versus Brex, Ramp Plus requires an additional platform fee on top of its $15 per-seat rate for advanced ERP integrations, whereas Brex Premium packages ERP integrations into a flat $12 per user per month rate."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Mercury Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Mercury provides business banking, company cards and corporate spend tools. Mercury provides up to $5M in FDIC insurance through partner banks and sweep networks. Mercury's base plan costs $0 per month with no minimum balance rules, no overdraft fees, and free ACH payments, checks, domestic wires and USD international wire transfers. Mercury includes company debit and credit cards with built-in expense management rules. Mercury Treasury access opens for accounts maintaining a balance of $250,000 or more.\n\nMercury Plus costs $29.90 per month, with a 30-day free trial. It adds recurring invoicing, unlimited 1099 filings, priority support, and invoice processing with ACH debits at $1 per transaction. Mercury Pro costs $299 per month, which reduces ACH debit invoice fees to $0 and assigns a dedicated relationship manager. Optional add-ons include Mercury Books at $35 per month and Mercury Payroll at $100 per month plus $50 per person paid per month, with both fees waived through December 31, 2026. Mercury charges a 1% currency exchange fee on non-USD transactions.\n\nWorked cost example: Over 12 months, Mercury base costs $0 in software fees. Mercury Plus costs $29.90 multiplied by 12, which equals $358.80 per year. Mercury Pro costs $299 multiplied by 12, which equals $3,588 per year. On Brex Premium, a 10-person team pays $1,440 per year ($12 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12), while 10 users pay $0 on Brex Essentials. These calculations show list-price arithmetic, not binding quotes.\n\nMercury fits businesses that want commercial checking, high FDIC sweep limits and company cards under one flat monthly price. Versus Brex, Mercury is a banking platform rather than a dedicated multi-entity expense suite, charging $29.90 or $299 per month for advanced invoicing tiers, whereas Brex provides specialized global spend controls and human resources information system (HRIS) connections."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Expensify Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Expensify focuses on expense reporting, receipt capture, card tracking and employee reimbursements. The Submit plan costs $0 and is free for all members, providing SmartScan receipt reading, mileage tracking and basic expense report generation. Expensify Collect costs $5 per member per month and includes employee reimbursements, corporate card management, expense and travel approval workflows, travel booking, and integrations with QuickBooks Online and Xero.\n\nExpensify Control features custom pricing that Expensify advertises as low as $9 per member per month, supported by a 30-day free trial. Control adds multi-level approval hierarchies, corporate budgeting, Security Assertion Markup Language (SAML) Single Sign-On (SSO), and integrations with advanced ERP systems including NetSuite and Sage Intacct.\n\nWorked cost example: A team of 10 members on Expensify Collect pays $5 multiplied by 10 members multiplied by 12 months, totaling $600 per year. That same 10-person team on Brex Premium pays $1,440 per year ($12 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12), making Expensify Collect $840 cheaper annually for core expense handling. If the team needs advanced approval flows on Expensify Control at the advertised starting rate of $9 per member per month, the annual cost is $9 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12, which equals $1,080 per year. This arithmetic uses published list prices and is not a formal quote.\n\nExpensify fits organizations prioritizing receipt scanning, employee expense reimbursements and travel management."
    },
    {
      "heading": "BILL Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "BILL specializes in financial operations automation, covering accounts payable and corporate spend management. Its subscription pricing divides into Essentials at $49 per user per month, Team at $65 per user per month, and Corporate at $89 per user per month, with Enterprise pricing quoted separately. Essentials connects with accounting software via manual CSV file import and export, while Team and Corporate provide automatic bidirectional accounting synchronization. For borrowing, BILL advertises commercial credit lines ranging from $1,000 to $5,000,000.\n\nTransaction fees on BILL include $0.59 per payment and $1.99 per payment when BILL prints and mails a paper check, with other transaction fees not individually labeled on the reviewed page text. Separately, the page states that BILL Spend & Expense charges no per-user subscription fees.\n\nWorked cost example: For 10 users on BILL Essentials, the annual subscription is $49 multiplied by 10 users multiplied by 12 months, which equals $5,880 per year. On BILL Team, 10 users cost $65 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12, or $7,800 per year. On BILL Corporate, 10 users cost $89 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12, which equals $10,680 per year. In comparison, Brex Premium for 10 users totals $1,440 per year ($12 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12), and Brex Essentials totals $0. BILL Spend & Expense lists no per-user fees, matching Brex Essentials at $0. This arithmetic reflects list rates and does not constitute a formal quote.\n\nBILL fits organizations that handle heavy invoice processing and accounts payable workflows requiring automated check mailing. Versus Brex, BILL charges higher per-seat software fees on its primary Accounts Payable tiers ($49 to $89 per user per month compared to Brex Premium at $12), and its entry tier relies on manual CSV imports rather than automatic accounting integrations."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Relay Pricing, Plans and Fit",
      "body": "Relay is an online business banking platform providing multi-account checking and card issuance. Relay accounts feature no minimum balance requirements, no overdraft fees and no hidden maintenance charges. All tiers include unlimited user seats, invoicing and direct accounting integrations.\n\nRelay Starter costs $0 per month and includes up to 20 checking accounts per business, 50 credit and debit cards, an APY of 1.19% on savings (footnoted), and 1% cash back on credit card transactions (footnoted). Relay Grow costs $30 per month ($360 per year) and introduces multi-step approval workflows, recurring invoices, bookkeeping automations, 1.87% APY on savings, and 1.25% credit card cash back. Relay Scale displays a regular rate of $120 per month shown alongside a $90 per month figure, providing 50 checking accounts, 3.21% APY on savings, 1.5% cash back, and fee-free same-day ACH transfers. \n\nWorked cost example: Over 12 months, Relay Starter costs $0 in account fees, while Relay Grow costs $30 multiplied by 12, totaling $360 per year. Relay Scale at the displayed $90 figure costs $1,080 per year ($90 multiplied by 12), or $1,440 per year at the $120 figure ($120 multiplied by 12). A 10-person team on Brex Premium costs $1,440 per year ($12 multiplied by 10 multiplied by 12), while Brex Essentials costs $0. These comparisons represent arithmetic on listed prices, not binding quotes.\n\nRelay fits small businesses that want multiple distinct checking accounts to organize cash flow alongside interest-bearing savings. Versus Brex, Relay does not offer an international multi-entity expense platform or custom ERP integrations like NetSuite, focusing instead on domestic business banking and sub-account management."
    }
  ],
  "stillBetterFit": {
    "heading": "When Brex Is Still the Better Fit",
    "body": "Brex remains the closer match for companies operating across international entities that require global card programs and advanced corporate spend policies. Brex Essentials costs $0 per user per month and provides global card acceptance, one local card program, support for up to two legal entities, bill pay, employee reimbursements, accounting integrations, travel booking, local currency wires and application programming interface (API) access.\n\nBrex Premium at $12 per user per month introduces dynamic expense review chains, multiple customizable expense policies, multi-entity support across United States and international entities, live budget tracking, and integrations with enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems and human resources information systems (HRIS). For larger teams, Brex offers custom Enterprise and Smart Card options. Brex LLC operates as a wholly owned subsidiary of Capital One, N.A., and displays variable annualized estimated treasury return figures ranging from 3.63% to 3.98%.\n\nOrganizations needing complex multi-country approval rules find those capabilities directly inside Brex Premium without stitching separate card and expense systems together.\n\nWho This Is Not For\n\n- Sole proprietors and very small teams that only need straightforward domestic checking with sub-accounts; Relay Starter provides 20 checking accounts and cards for $0 per month.\n- Companies that want an integrated commercial bank account with $5M in FDIC sweep coverage and free domestic wires; Mercury base provides those banking services for $0 per month.\n- Businesses looking strictly for accounts payable check printing and mailing; BILL specializes in AP disbursements with mailed checks priced at $1.99.\n- Organizations seeking simple employee receipt scanning and mileage logging without corporate credit cards; Expensify Submit costs $0 for basic reporting.\n\nWhat Would Change Our Answer\n\n- Brex increasing the $12 per user per month Premium rate or adding per-seat charges to Brex Essentials.\n- Ramp altering its Free plan features or eliminating the 20% annual billing discount on Ramp Plus.\n- Mercury introducing monthly account maintenance fees on its base plan or altering its $250,000 balance threshold for Mercury Treasury.\n- Expensify adjusting its $5 per member per month Collect rate or changing its 30-day trial rules on Control.\n- BILL introducing mandatory per-user subscription fees on BILL Spend & Expense.\n- Relay changing its 50-card allowance on Starter or adjusting its 1.19% to 3.21% savings APY tiers."
  },
  "verdict": "Brex provides corporate cards, spend management and global entity support with an entry plan at $0 per user per month and Premium at $12 per user per month. Ramp Free offers a comparable $0 per user corporate card and bill pay platform, while Ramp Plus costs $15 per user per month plus a team platform fee. Mercury provides $0 business checking with up to $5M in FDIC insurance and company cards, Relay offers up to 50 sub-accounts with savings yields up to 3.21% APY, Expensify Collect charges $5 per member per month for expense reporting, and BILL automates accounts payable starting at $49 per user per month.\n\nTo pick a Brex alternative, calculate your total user seat count, verify whether your business needs multi-entity ERP integrations or basic business checking, and compare the published rates in the table above.",
